Identify the Issue: While User_Name is provided, there are no unique Customer_ID fields or transaction timestamps to reliably track repeat purchases versus duplicate name entries.

How it affects analysis: It prevents accurate cohort analysis, customer lifetime value estimation, and distinction between new and returning buyers.

How it was handled: I focused demographic and spend analysis on per-transaction order metrics (Average Order Value) rather than user-level retention metrics.


PART 2: ADDITIONAL ANALYSIS LIMITATIONS & UNSAFE CONCLUSIONS

A. Two Limitations of Your Analysis:
Lack of Profit Margin : The dataset only tracks gross sales (Purchase_Amount), shipping fees, or return rates, net profitability cannot be directly calculated.
Missing Customer Acquisition & Marketing Spend Data: We cannot measure Return on Ad Spend (ROAS) or Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC) because advertising channels and campaign costs are not tracked.
B. One Conclusion That CANNOT Safely Be Made From Your Dataset:
Unsafe Conclusion: "Marketing campaigns on Instagram are failing because the Beauty category generated the lowest sales volume."
Why it is unsafe: The dataset contains zero information regarding marketing channels, ad spend, web traffic, or product review ratings.
Asserting a specific marketing failure without ad impression or click-through data would be an ungrounded assumption.
